WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.751
Dorothy pointed to some bright lights in the distance.

2
00:00:03.752 --> 00:00:07.097
"That must be the Emerald City," she said.

3
00:00:07.098 --> 00:00:10.814
"We'll reach it by noon," said the Scarecrow.

4
00:00:10.815 --> 00:00:14.252
As they walked, their excitement and fear grew.

5
00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:17.915
They were excited because the answer to their dreams was in sight.

6
00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:21.912
But they were worried because of what the woman had told them.

7
00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:25.783
She had never seen the Wizard of Oz.

8
00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:31.430
When they reached the city, they found the gate locked. Dorothy rang the bell.

9
00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:35.200
A man appeared and asked, "What do you want?"

10
00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:39.482
"We have come to see the Great Oz," answered Dorothy.

11
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:44.788
The man was so surprised by the answer that he fell down.

12
00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:48.643
"No one sees Oz," said the man.

13
00:00:48.644 --> 00:00:54.513
"He is a powerful and terrible wizard, and he dislikes being bothered."

14
00:00:54.514 --> 00:00:59.156
"We won't be a bother because our need is great," said the Scarecrow.

15
00:00:59.157 --> 00:01:04.564
"We have heard that the Great Oz is good," added Dorothy.

16
00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:08.171
"I will take you to his palace," said the man.

17
00:01:08.172 --> 00:01:11.620
"But you must wear these tinted glasses."

18
00:01:11.621 --> 00:01:14.602
"Tinted glasses?" asked Dorothy.

19
00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:16.751
"Yes," said the man.

20
00:01:16.752 --> 00:01:23.139
"Without them you would be blinded by the brilliance and brightness of the Emerald City."

21
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:29.842
Before Dorothy and her friends entered the city, each was fitted with tinted glasses, even Toto.

22
00:01:29.843 --> 00:01:34.794
The man led them to a great palace in the center of the city.

23
00:01:34.795 --> 00:01:41.383
"Here are strangers," he said to a soldier. "They demand to see the Great Oz."

24
00:01:41.384 --> 00:01:48.580
The soldier nodded. "Step inside. I will take your message to Oz."

25
00:01:48.581 --> 00:01:55.801
With that, he disappeared for a long time.

26
00:01:55.802 --> 00:01:59.655
"Have you seen Oz?" asked Dorothy when he returned.

27
00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:05.503
"No," replied the soldier. "I've never seen him. But I spoke with him.

28
00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:09.744
He will see each of you alone, and just one of you a day.

29
00:02:09.745 --> 00:02:12.761
You must wait in the palace until he calls you.

30
00:02:12.762 --> 00:02:21.947
Now you can go to your rooms."

31
00:02:21.948 --> 00:02:28.037
"Follow me," a girl said to Dorothy. "I will show you to your room."

32
00:02:28.038 --> 00:02:35.091
Dorothy followed the girl, who took her to a beautiful room with a fountain.

33
00:02:35.092 --> 00:02:38.484
"Oh, it is lovely," said Dorothy.

34
00:02:38.485 --> 00:02:44.382
"Make yourself at home," said the girl. "Oz will send for you tomorrow."

35
00:02:44.383 --> 00:02:48.692
The next morning the girl returned, and she helped Dorothy dress.

36
00:02:48.693 --> 00:02:52.653
She even tied a green ribbon around Toto's neck.

37
00:02:52.654 --> 00:02:56.995
"Are you really going to see Oz?" asked the girl shyly.

38
00:02:56.996 --> 00:03:02.271
"Of course," said Dorothy. "If he will see me."

39
00:03:02.272 --> 00:03:05.615
The girl led Dorothy through the palace.

40
00:03:05.616 --> 00:03:10.049
"What is your business?" demanded the soldier who stood outside the throne room.

41
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:16.163
Dorothy was quite surprised. "I am here to see Oz," she said uncertainly.

42
00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:20.607
"I spoke to you yesterday. Will he see me?"

43
00:03:20.608 --> 00:03:24.934
"He will," said the soldier. "He is not happy about it.

44
00:03:24.935 --> 00:03:29.373
But I told him about the silver shoes on your feet and the kiss upon your forehead.

45
00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:33.515
So he agreed to see you." A bell rang.

46
00:03:33.516 --> 00:03:36.222
"That is the signal," said the soldier.

47
00:03:36.223 --> 00:03:47.024
"You must go into the throne room alone."

48
00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:49.938
Dorothy walked in as bravely as she could.

49
00:03:49.939 --> 00:03:53.062
The room was both strange and wonderful.

50
00:03:53.063 --> 00:03:58.524
It was made of emeralds, and the light shining from above made everything sparkle.

51
00:03:58.525 --> 00:04:03.115
The throne itself was the strangest thing in the room.

52
00:04:03.116 --> 00:04:07.128
It was bigger than any chair Dorothy had ever seen.

53
00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:12.916
Floating just above it was a giant head with no body.

54
00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:19.809
As Dorothy looked at the head, its eyes opened and began to stare at her.

55
00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:26.134
"I am Oz," said the giant head. "Who are you and why do you seek me?"

56
00:04:26.135 --> 00:04:35.045
The voice wasn't as awful as Dorothy expected, so she bravely said, "I am Dorothy from Kansas. I need your help."

57
00:04:35.046 --> 00:04:40.370
"Before I help you," said Oz, "you must answer some questions.

58
00:04:40.371 --> 00:04:42.259
Will you tell the truth?"

59
00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:52.364
"Yes," answered Dorothy because she had no reason to lie.

